{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 1, :comments ["<b>And Jacob saw that there was grain in Egypt.</b> And from where did he see? For he did not see but rather heard, as it is said, ״הִנֵּה שָׁמַעְתִּי״ and so forth. And what is וַיַּרְא? He saw in the mirror of prophecy that there was still שֶׁבֶר for him in Egypt; but it was not actual prophecy to inform him explicitly that this was Joseph." "<b>Why do you look.</b> Why do you show yourselves before the sons of Ishmael and the sons of Esau as though you are sated? At that time they still had produce (Ta'anit 10). And to me its plain sense appears: לָמָּה תִּתְרָאוּ — why should everyone gaze at you and wonder at you, that you do not seek food for yourselves before what is in your hands is exhausted. And from others I have heard that it is an expression of anxiety: why should you be anxious about the famine — similar to it: וּמַרְוֶה גַּם הוּא יוֹרֵא (Proverbs 11)."], :book :genesis, :voice :rashi, :lang :en, :chapter 42, :notes {}, :source-witnesses nil, :timestamp "2026-08-02T09:03:08.104976019Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}